The reason for this is in the [gpio_pin_get_config](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/doxygen/html/group__gpio__interface.html#ga133284b60a13c6dc50b87c1d04259f5e)
 The gpio_pin_get_config()  [zephyr/include/zephyr/drivers/gpio.h](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/352fde1271c568fa24cb48b4aed20f97b25945b1/include/zephyr/drivers/gpio.h#L881-L883) return code is _not_ ENOTSUP 
```
	if (api->pin_get_config == NULL)
		return -ENOSYS;
```

If getting current pin configuration is not implemented by the driver, then we should not run this test. Returning fail will remind us there might be a  problem or not running the test next time if it is as expected, while returning pass will cover the problem. @FRASTM 

I think we can just remove the following lines
``` 
	if (rc == -ENOTSUP) {
		return TC_PASS;
	}
```
